  "content": {
    "id": "p40-q63-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "63",
    "prompt": "Solve the equation for $0\\leq\\theta\\leq2\\pi$:\n$$\\cos\\left(\\theta-\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)+\\sin\\left(\\theta+\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2-\\sqrt3}}.$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\theta=\\dfrac{7\\pi}{12},\\dfrac{23\\pi}{12}$.\n\nTransform the left-hand side to $\\sqrt{2+\\sqrt3}\\cos(\\theta-\\frac{\\pi}{4})$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\cos\\left(\\theta-\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)+\\sin\\left(\\theta+\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)&=\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}\\cos\\theta+\\frac12\\sin\\theta+\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}\\sin\\theta+\\frac12\\cos\\theta\\\\\\cos\\left(\\theta-\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)+\\sin\\left(\\theta+\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)&=\\frac{\\sqrt3+1}{2}(\\cos\\theta+\\sin\\theta)\\\\\\cos\\left(\\theta-\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)+\\sin\\left(\\theta+\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)&=\\frac{\\sqrt3+1}{\\sqrt2}\\cos\\left(\\theta-\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)\\\\\\cos\\left(\\theta-\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)+\\sin\\left(\\theta+\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)&=\\sqrt{2+\\sqrt3}\\cos\\left(\\theta-\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right).\\end{align*}$$\nSince $(2-\\sqrt3)(2+\\sqrt3)=1$,\n$$\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2-\\sqrt3}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{2+\\sqrt3}}{2}.$$\nThe equation becomes\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sqrt{2+\\sqrt3}\\cos\\left(\\theta-\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)&=\\frac{\\sqrt{2+\\sqrt3}}{2}\\\\\\cos\\left(\\theta-\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)&=\\frac12.\\end{align*}$$\nSince $-\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\leq\\theta-\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\leq\\frac{7\\pi}{4}$,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\theta-\\frac{\\pi}{4}&=\\frac{\\pi}{3},\\frac{5\\pi}{3}\\\\\\theta&=\\frac{7\\pi}{12},\\frac{23\\pi}{12}.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
